# Presentation boundaries

- UI and presentation code binds domain snapshots and events; it does not
  calculate damage, economy, wave results, save settlement, or run rules.
- Follow `UI-SPEC.md`: authored prefab shells, inspector-dragged references,
  TMP text, layout groups, fixed slots for fixed counts, and bindable prefab
  view hierarchies for variable lists.
- UI controllers subscribe to domain events and refresh from a bind method.
  Do not poll gameplay state every frame unless the UI contract explicitly
  requires a world-space follow update.
- Animate changing values with LitMotion. Do not use coroutines, `Update`, or
  DOTween for presentation animation.
- Verify UI changes through prefab/scene wiring and Unity console inspection.
  Do not claim rendered or Play Mode behavior from EditMode tests alone.
